{
  "id": "T-297",
  "title": "Remove the spec preflight, and have the worker read the spec and the code in its first round, then ask or plan before it writes code",
  "public_title": "Remove the spec preflight and let the worker plan first",
  "milestone": "M2",
  "depends_on": [],
  "scope": [
    "bin/**",
    "skills/**",
    "design/design.md",
    "tests/**",
    "design/tasks/T-297.json"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "Why. The spec preflight (a review of each spec by a fresh model before dispatch) never settles: one task (T-285) took eleven passes, and in one evening six specs used up their passes and raised the captain card that asks what to do next (the pass budget card). Each pass finds new points and pulls code detail back into short specs. The worker reads the code anyway and finds real mismatches better (captain, 2026-10-11).",
    "What, no preflight. The spec preflight is removed: there are no preflight rounds and no pass budget card. No step requires a SPEC-OK record any more: pinning, repinning, worker dispatch, the release of the hold on a task that has used up its worker rounds (the round-budget hold) by a later repin, and pull-request publication through the older path that publishes a pull request for a task with no pin (the legacy stock path). A task held by the round budget today is released by an approved repin alone. The captain's dispatch card stays the approval of what to build and why.",
    "What, read first. In its first round on a new task, and in its first round after a repin, the worker reads the spec and the code before it changes any file.",
    "What, ask or plan. When the spec is unclear, does not match the code, changes a rule but does not say what happens to records and tasks already in flight, or lists `design/design.md` without naming the numbered section it edits, the worker asks through the existing question path and stops; otherwise it writes a short plan (files it will change, how it proves done) into its round report and goes on in the same round.",
    "What, work already in flight. Existing pins, running workers, open pull requests and stored preflight records keep working, a spec with a SPEC-GAPS record pins normally, and an answer to any leftover preflight pass-budget card changes nothing.",
    "What, removal. The preflight launcher, its prompt, its pass budget and their tests are deleted; the code that reads and checks stored preflight records stays, and the board's display of old preflight crew rows is unchanged. `bin/fm-review.sh --spec-preflight` (with or without `--card` or `--pr-authoring`) exits non-zero and prints one line saying that the worker's first round now checks the spec.",
    "What, what moves. Every check the preflight ran on a submitted spec before the reviewer, including the external public-field checks (numbers glued to words, slash chains, a valid `public_title`) and the `adopt` validation, moves to pin time and keeps refusing there. The reviewer's rewording of dispatch cards, repin cards and pull-request drafts goes away; cards keep the check-plain check at request time and drafts keep the plain-text checks at sealing.",
    "Docs, skills. `skills/firstmate/SKILL.md`, `skills/worker/SKILL.md` and `skills/reviewer/SKILL.md` describe the new flow.",
    "Docs, plain writing. `skills/firstmate/plain-writing.md` says the external public-field checks run at pin time.",
    "Docs, design §6. `design/design.md` replaces the §6 \"Spec preflight and migration\" subsection with the worker's first-round plan and drops the preflight step from the repin sequence in the §6 \"Small changes\" subsection.",
    "Docs, other design sections. `design/design.md` drops or rewrites the preflight sentences in §5.2, §5.4, §7, §8, §11, §12, §13.2, §15.2 and §15.7.",
    "Docs, inventory. `skills/firstmate/rule-inventory.json` is updated for every rule sentence added, moved or deleted in `skills/firstmate/SKILL.md` (such as R-157, R-158, R-174, R-190 and R-191), and for every entry whose evidence file is deleted (such as R-190, which cites `bin/lib/fm_preflight_budget.py`).",
    "Done, tests. New tests prove: a spec with no preflight record pins and dispatches (`dispatch: no preflight needed`, fail-first); the first-round instructions tell the worker to read the spec and code, then ask or write a plan before changing files (`worker: plans before code`, fail-first); external public fields are still checked at pin time (`pin: external public fields checked`, regression); the old preflight command fails with the pointer line (`preflight: removed with pointer`, fail-first); a task pinned with an old SPEC-OK record still dispatches (`preflight: old records still accepted`, regression); a task held by the round budget is released by an approved repin with no SPEC-OK record (`round budget: repin alone releases`, fail-first); a spec whose bytes have a SPEC-GAPS record pins and dispatches (`preflight: old gaps record does not block`, fail-first); the first round after a repin gets the same read-first instructions (`worker: plans after repin`, fail-first)."
  ],
  "explain": {
    "en": {
      "intent": [
        {"kind": "fact", "text": "A spec pins and dispatches with no preflight record."},
        {"kind": "fact", "text": "In its first round, the worker checks the spec against the code."},
        {"kind": "fact", "text": "Old records and open tasks stay valid."}
      ],
      "why": [
        {"kind": "fact", "text": "The preflight never settles and asks for code detail."}
      ],
      "scope_in": ["the preflight code and its tests", "the worker's first round", "skills and the design doc"],
      "scope_out": ["the PR review", "the captain's dispatch card"],
      "done": [
        {"kind": "fact", "text": "Intent 1: a test shows a spec dispatches with no preflight."},
        {"kind": "fact", "text": "Intent 2: a test shows a plan or question comes before code."},
        {"kind": "fact", "text": "Intent 3: a test shows an old SPEC-OK task still dispatches."}
      ],
      "notes": [
        {"kind": "caution", "text": "This task is the last one checked by the old preflight."}
      ],
      "before_nodes": [
        {"state": "gone", "label": "Preflight passes"},
        {"state": "same", "label": "Captain approves"},
        {"state": "same", "label": "Worker builds"}
      ],
      "after_nodes": [
